# Documentation maintenance

When a change affects user-visible behavior, update the matching `docs/` source in the same change. Then run `npm run docs:build` and commit `AI-SUPPORT.md`. Do not edit `AI-SUPPORT.md` by hand.

- New or renamed control, toast, or command → `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/reference.md`, and `docs/FAQ.md`
- New or changed setting → `docs/configuration.md` and `docs/reference.md`
- New error or a changed CLI failure path → `docs/troubleshooting.md` and `docs/symptom-index.md`
- Changed persistence, selection, or refresh rules → `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/reference.md`
- Install, package, or debug steps → `docs/getting-started.md` and `docs/development.md`
- Removed behavior → delete it from the docs and from the FAQ. Do not leave it as if it still exists.
- A limitation or non-goal → `docs/roadmap.md` and `docs/product.md`

`npm run docs:check` must pass. It compares `AI-SUPPORT.md` to the generator output and does not rebuild the file.

Do not document OpenSpec, Cursor, or VS Code features this extension does not implement. Link to https://openspec.dev/docs instead of copying their manual.
